# Working with Beocat

In order to deploy OpenMP- and MPI-enabled programs non-interactively requires a bit of work.

Below are some template "SLURM Scripts" for OMP, MPI, and Hybrid applications.

## OMP 

```
#!/bin/bash
#SBATCH --job-name=test
#SBATCH --account=<account_name>
#SBATCH --partition=<partition_name>
#SBATCH --nodes=1            # physical compute node
#SBATCH --ntasks-per-node=1  # processes/ranks per node
#SBATCH --cpus-per-task=4    # physical core per process (for threads)
# Wall clock limit:
#SBATCH --time=00:00:30
## Command(s) to run (example):
export OMP_NUM_THREADS=$SLURM_CPUS_PER_TASK
./a.out
```

## MPI 

```
#!/bin/bash
#SBATCH --job-name=test
#SBATCH --account=<account_name>
#SBATCH --partition=<partition_name>
#SBATCH --ntasks=40
#SBATCH --cpus-per-task=1
#SBATCH --time=00:00:30
module load foss
mpirun ./a.out
```

